From: seat usb-xhci (koru-desktop)
Subject: ukboot: cast init_array ctor call to the arg-taking signature

lib/ukboot/boot.c calls `(*ctorfn)(argc, argv)` on entries typed
`uk_ctor_func_t` = `void (*)()` (include/uk/ctors.h:45). Modern clang
(C23 semantics for `()` — no longer "unspecified args") rejects the
two-argument call: `too many arguments to function '*ctorfn'`.
Cast at the call site so the argc/argv convention survives without
changing the typedef or the ABI of the ctor table itself.

Upstream status: not yet submitted (COCPORN fork working tree).
---
 lib/ukboot/boot.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
diff --git a/lib/ukboot/boot.c b/lib/ukboot/boot.c
index abbb394f..141a9d02 100644
--- a/lib/ukboot/boot.c
+++ b/lib/ukboot/boot.c
@@ -486,7 +486,7 @@ int do_main(int argc, char *argv[])
 
 		uk_pr_debug("Call constructor: %p(%d, %p)...\n", *ctorfn,
 			    argc, argv);
-		(*ctorfn)(argc, argv);
+		(*(void (*)(int, char **))*ctorfn)(argc, argv);
 	}
 
 #if CONFIG_LIBUKPRINT_KLVL_INFO
